+### Composer placeholder
+
+`ComposerPlaceholder` supplies faint placeholder text for an empty session composer. Use it for a suggestion the user
+can accept, such as the next prompt. The host shows the first non-empty contribution in `order`, then contribution
+order. Typing replaces the placeholder, and the text is not part of the draft until you write it with
+`screen.composer.setText`.
+
+`show` returns the text for one session, or `undefined` to show none. The host runs it for the routed composer, and
+again when what it reads changes. Return `undefined` while the composer has text, because the placeholder is only
+visible when the draft is empty:
+
+```tsx
+import { ComposerPlaceholder } from "@opencode/plugin/gui"
+
+ctx.add(ComposerPlaceholder, {
+  id: "next-prompt",
+  show: ({ session, screen }) => {
+    if (screen.composer.text().trim()) return
+    return nextPrompt(session.id)
+  },
+})
+```
+
+#### Reference
+
+```ts
+interface ComposerPlaceholder {
+  id: string
+  order?: number
+  show(input: ComposerPlaceholderProps): string | undefined
+}
+
+interface ComposerPlaceholderProps {
+  session: MountedSession
+  screen: SessionScreen
+}
+```
+
 ### Code blocks
 
 `CodeBlock` renders the fenced code blocks of the languages you list as your own UI, in place of the highlighted code.
